 short cabaña stay","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["Tropical/Beaches","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"Tropical/Beaches":"evidenced","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed","si_raw":"Tropical/Beaches","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Tropical/Beaches'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Castaway-island overnight cabaña","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotels-g298434-San_Blas_Islands_Guna_Yala_Region-Hotels.html","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"DMC cabaña package or private charter overnight","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["DMC","package"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Isla Perro (Dog Island) wreck snorkel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://sanblasadventures.com/san-blas-snorkeling/","si":"expedition","commission":"day tour / charter stop","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Panama → Cartagena sailing charter (3–5 days)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://sanblasadventures.com/boat-colombia-to-panama/general-information/","si":"expedition","commission":"charter / CLIA lane — highest-value bookable in region","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Guna mola textiles + living culture (1925 revolution, matrilineal congress, Dulegaya)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage (future)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/culture-cuisine/indigenous-communities/guna/","timing":"dry season Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"dry season Dec–Apr","commission":"cultural add-on / community visit via DMC (direct artisan purchases non-commissionable)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["Culture & Heritage (future)","culture"],"shelf_fit":{"Culture & Heritage (future)":"evidenced","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"Culture & Heritage (future)","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Culture & Heritage (future)'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in San Blas?","a":"Remoteness, not crime. There is no hospital and, on most cays, no clinic; serious illness or injury means evacuation to Panama City or the US, which can exceed $50,000. Comprehensive travel + medevac insurance is a condition of going, not an option — and dengue/malaria risk is year-round.","source":"smartraveller.gov.au, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the boat crossings and the 4x4 access road dangerous?","a":"Manageable but weather-governed. Everything moves by open boat, so insist on worn life vests, a licensed captain, and a real forecast check; the Colombia passage is 24–52 hours at open sea with no turning back mid-crossing. The overland Cartí route is a steep, rain-sensitive mountain road needing a 4x4 (4–5 hours). Guided only.","source":"sanblasadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Which San Blas islands are best for beaches and snorkeling?","a":"The outer Cayos Holandeses (Dutch Cays) are widely rated the best snorkeling in the archipelago, with healthy reef and cushion starfish on the flats. Isla Perro holds the signature shallow-shipwreck snorkel a few metres from shore, while the Cayos Limones lagoon (Isla Pelícano, of *Money Heist* fame) offers the easiest crystal-shallow day-trip.","source":"seasanblas.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is San Blas good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, if you want elemental over polished. The set-piece is a private or near-private sand-cay cabaña — hammock, palm, reef at the doorstep, no wifi — from ~$56–$100/night full-board, scaling up to a private crewed catamaran overnight. Expect solar power and often no running water: this is the Caribbean before anyone built a lobby on it.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What is the Panama-to-Cartagena sailing trip like?","a":"It''s a genuine passage, not a lagoon cruise. Three days threading the San Blas cays, then 24–52 hours of open-water crossing to Colombia; shared cabins run ~$525–$750 (meals + immigration paperwork included), private from ~$900+. Small boats have limited cabins and sell out weeks ahead for dry-season departures.","source":"sanblasadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Who are the Guna, and how do I enter the comarca?","a":"You enter on Guna terms. The Guna are a matrilineal people who won semi-autonomy in the 1925 revolution and still govern by congress under saila leaders; entry means a passport check and a per-person cash fee (~$20/foreigner) at the Cartí checkpoint, with no ATMs on the islands. Buy reverse-appliqué molas direct from the women who sew them.","source":"ampatours.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Blas Islands (Guna Yala), Panama — Castaway Cays, Sailing & the Guna | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-PA","local_keywords":["San Blas Guna Yala","islas San Blas Panamá","velero San Blas Cartagena","cómo llegar a San Blas desde Ciudad de Panamá","cabañas San Blas Guna Yala","molas guna","Cayos Holandeses"],"hreflang":["en","es-PA"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama","read":"2026-08-20T14:55:13Z","source_updated":"2025-12-10T13:26:25+00:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07","long_tail":["how to get to San Blas islands from Panama City","San Blas to Cartagena sailing trip","best San Blas islands for snorkeling","Isla Perro shipwreck snorkel","private catamaran charter San Blas","is San Blas Panama safe"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"type":"private crewed catamaran","name":"ZENITH / CruiseSanBlas / Charter in San Blas","note":"the luxury vehicle in Guna Yala — no branded ultra property exists","earning":"private-charter / CLIA lane"},{"type":"Panama City bookend hotel","name":"American Trade Hotel (Casco Viejo, Small Luxury Hotels of the World)","note":"consortia/Virtuoso-adjacent luxury anchor for the city night","earning":"Fora / consortia hotel commission"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Blas / Guna Yala, Panama, Panama"},"geo":{"lat":9.57,"lng":-78.95},"orbit":[{"id":"bocas-del-toro-panama","jewels":13,"si":["tropical","diveglobal","romance","adventure"]},{"id":"