]","commission":"food/cultural experience affiliate + retail","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Chiapa de Corzo (UNESCO / Pueblo Mágico)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Chiapas-attractions/Sumidero-Canyon-National-Park/d5506-a14134","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"paired with Sumidero day tour (DMC/affiliate, live)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Sumidero Canyon boat cruise","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","hook":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","si":"expedition","blurb":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","commission":"guided boat tour commissionable (live); park/boat federal fee non-commissionable","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Lagos de Montebello","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"guided long-day tour DMC (live) — keep to established tourist route near border","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"El Chiflón waterfalls","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","si":"expedition","commission":"guided day tour DMC/affiliate (live) + entrance non-commissionable","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"El Arcotete / Rancho Nuevo","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"local guide/transfer affiliate + entrance (live)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Temazcal + boutique-casa spa evenings","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"http://www.casadelalmahotelboutiqueandspa.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"hotel + spa package direct/DMC (live)","wells":["activities","shop"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","package","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the road dangerous?","a":"The connective road is the risk, not the city. Highway 199 between San Cristóbal and Palenque via Ocosingo has reported armed robberies (predominantly at night) plus periodic CNTE union blockades that usually cause only short delays. The rule is daytime-only overland travel with a vetted guide or private transfer, never a night self-drive; the city center itself is pedestrian-comfortable by day.","source":"aboutsancristobal.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are San Juan Chamula and Zinacantán, and how do I visit respectfully?","a":"They are living Tzotzil Maya villages, 10 km out, and a guide is effectively mandatory. Chamula''s church is a pine-needle-floored space of Maya-Catholic fusion with ritual healings day and night and a strict no-photography rule inside; Zinacantán (99% Indigenous) is a backstrap-loom weaving town with a women''s co-op. Pay the community fees and follow a guide who knows the etiquette.","source":"wandersmiles.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is there to do in the city itself?","a":"Walk the pedestrian andadores — Real de Guadalupe and the Andador Eclesiástico — between two hillside churches. The Templo de Santo Domingo has Chiapas''s most elaborate carved pink facade with a Tzotzil/Tzeltal textile market at its churchyard, and the Museo del Ámbar (in the ex-convent of La Merced) shows amber with 25-million-year-old inclusions, alongside a strong Chiapas-coffee and cacao café culture.","source":"randomtrip.net, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is Sumidero Canyon, and is it worth it?","a":"Yes — it''s the region''s signature nature outing. A 2-hour open-boat cruise from the UNESCO colonial town of Chiapa de Corzo runs ~32 km beneath canyon walls up to ~1,000 m, past waterfalls and wildlife. It''s a low-risk daytime trip with licensed operators — life vests on, weather-dependent.","source":"voyagemexique.info, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is San Cristóbal a good base for a quiet, cultured couple''s trip?","a":"Yes — it''s cultured romance, not resort romance. At 2,200 m the highland evenings ask for a sweater; boutique colonial casas like Hotel Bö and Casa del Alma offer temazcal spa culture and courtyard dinners along cobblestone andadores. Come in the dry season (Nov–April), with crisp 18–24°C days, blue skies and minimal rain.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Does the altitude affect visitors?","a":"Only mildly. At ~2,200 m some travelers feel light shortness of breath or a disturbed first night''s sleep, but it is not a serious altitude risk — hydrate and ease into exertion on day one. Drink bottled water only; dengue is a lowland concern (Palenque, the canyon), not the cool highland city.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico: Highland Chiapas, Maya Culture & Sumidero Canyon | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San Cristóbal de las Casas","Cañón del Sumidero","San Juan Chamula","Zinacantán tejido","Lagos de Montebello","El Chiflón cascadas","hoteles boutique San Cristóbal","mejor época para viajar a Chiapas","es seguro San Cristóbal de las Casas"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","primary_keyword":"San Cristóbal de las Casas","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel Bö","tier":"design-luxury boutique (not global 5-star)","earning":"Fora/Virtuoso consortia commission where participating; else bedbank/OTA","mor":true},{"name":"Casa del Alma Hotel Boutique & Spa","tier":"upper-mid spa boutique","earning":"consortia/agency commission or bedbank","mor":true},{"name":"Hotel Na Bolom","tier":"mid heritage/character","earning":"direct/OTA thin commission, high narrative value","mor":true},{"name":"Private-DMC program (Plan South America / bespoke)","tier":"ultra ground handle incl. private charter SC<->Palenque ~40min","earning":"MoR on itinerary not bed","mor":true}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":16.737,"lng":-92.6376},"orbit":[{"id":"palenque-mexico","jewels":10,"si":["culture","expedition"]}],"orbit_country":["akumal-mexico","bacalar-mexico","balandra-beach-mexico","cabo-pulmo-mexico","cabo-san-lucas-mexico","calakmul-mexico","campeche-city-mexico","cancun-mexico","careyes-mexico","celestun-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","chichen-itza-mexico","coba-mexico","costalegre-mexico","cozumel-mexico","east-cape-mexico","ensenada-mexico","espiritu-santo-island-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","holbox-mexico","huatulco-mexico","isla-contoy-mexico","isla-mujeres-mexico","izamal-mexico","la-paz-mexico","loreto-mexico","los-barriles-mexico","magdalena-bay-mexico","mahahual-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","merida-mexico","mexico-city-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","playa-del-carmen-mexico","puerto-aventuras-mexico","puerto-morelos-mexico","puerto-vallarta-mexico","punta-mita-mexico","rio-lagartos-mexico","san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","sayulita-mexico","sian-kaan-mexico","teotihuacan-mexico","tlaquepaque-mexico","todos-santos-mexico","tulum-mexico","uxmal-mexico","valladolid-mexico","valle-de-guadalupe-mexico","puerto-escondido-mexico"]}'::jsonb, 102),
  ('san-ignacio-belize', '10S', 'San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize', 'Belize', 'Belize''s inland adventure capital', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Belize', '{"expedition","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Base for Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — a guided-only Maya sacrificial cave holding the calcified ''Crystal Maiden'' skeleton near San Ignacio, Cayo District.","Xunantunich''s El Castillo (~40 m) is Belize''s 2nd-tallest structure; reached by a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry ~20 min from town.","Caracol''s Caana pyramid (141 ft / 43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure; access via military-escorted convoy from Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (~9 am) due to Guatemala-border proximity.","Blancaneaux Lodge, a ~20-room hideaway in the Mountain Pine Ridge, was bought by Francis Ford Coppola in the early 1980s and opened to guests in 1993.","BZE (Belize International) to San Ignacio is a ~2-hour drive west on the Western/George Price Highway; the Cayo caves are accessible year-round."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (verify)","hospital":"San Ignacio Community Hospital (local); trauma to Belize City (~2 hrs) or air-medical evac to Belize City / Guatemala City (verify)","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE -> San Ignacio ~2 hr drive, Western/George Price Highway; regional airstrip Maya Flats (verify)","guatemala_border_note":"Caracol requires military-escorted convoy; Xunantunich near border — disclose, verify current","malaria":"CDC: malaria a risk in SOME parts of Belize; treat mainland jungle as potential risk, advise travel-medicine consult","dengue":"present; mosquito-bite avoidance essential","vaccines":"Hepatitis A (all 1+), typhoid (rural/smaller-city) recommended","water":"bottled/treated only; avoid swimming in fresh unchlorinated water (leptospirosis) — ATM/cave-tubing are unavoidable-immersion guided activities","founder_policy_note":"only Southside Belize C