"evidenced","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Doka Estate coffee tour","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/san-jose-coffee-tours-2026-doka-estate-best-farms.htm (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Costa Rica''s oldest continuously operating coffee plantation, 70-hectare farm, ~1.5 hrs from San José, seedling-to-cup with bilingual guides; classic ~$25–35, premium cupping ~$65","si":"culture","blurb":"Costa Rica''s oldest continuously operating coffee plantation, 70-hectare farm, ~1.5 hrs from San José, seedling-to-cup with bilingual guides; classic ~$25–35, premium cupping ~$65","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable tour (Viator/ANYWHERE/DMC)","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Café Britt coffee tour","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/san-jose-coffee-tours-2026-doka-estate-best-farms.htm (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the polished, theatrical coffee-education show near Heredia; standard ~$32, barista experience ~$75. The entertainment-first alternative to Doka''s authenticity-first","si":"culture","blurb":"the polished, theatrical coffee-education show near Heredia; standard ~$32, barista experience ~$75. The entertainment-first alternative to Doka''s authenticity-first","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable tour","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Sarchí oxcart crafts","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/san-jose/tours/Poas-Volcano-Doka-Coffee-Plantation-and-La-Paz.php (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the town that hand-paints the carreta, Costa Rica''s national-symbol oxcart; the world''s largest oxcart and the artisan workshops. Usually stacked with Poás/Doka/Grecia","si":"culture","blurb":"the town that hand-paints the carreta, Costa Rica''s national-symbol oxcart; the world''s largest oxcart and the artisan workshops. Usually stacked with Poás/Doka/Grecia","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable combo day-tour + retail","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities","shop"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is San José worth staying a night, or just an airport?","a":"Worth a night. It''s the front door, not the destination — but the Pre-Columbian Gold Museum (~1,600 pieces, beside the Teatro Nacional), a three-museum pass (~$33), and the Barrio Escalante restaurant row give a genuine half-to-full day of culture-and-coffee substance.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can you day-trip Poás and Irazú volcanoes from San José?","a":"Yes — both are same-day from the capital. Irazú tops 3,432 m with both oceans visible on a clear morning; Poás runs a dynamic-access, online-only timed-entry model via SINAC, so go guided to absorb the timed-entry and closure logistics.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where is SJO airport and how busy does it get?","a":"Juan Santamaría (SJO) is Costa Rica''s primary international gateway, 20 km northwest of downtown in Alajuela. It just set a record, handling 3,215,208 international passengers between Nov 2025 and Apr 5 2026 — up 7.9% year-over-year — so book gateway beds and transfers ahead of the dry-season wave.","source":"ticotimes.net, 2026-07-06","si_tag":null},{"q":"If something goes wrong in Costa Rica, is medical care nearby?","a":"Reassuringly, yes — San José IS the national medical and evacuation hub. Hospital Clínica Bíblica (founded 1929, JCI-accredited, 24/7, with an on-site heliport for evac) and the US-affiliated Hospital CIMA are both in the metro, so serious care and the evac hub are right here.","source":"internationalinsurance.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San José & Costa Rica''s Central Valley: Volcanoes, Coffee Tours & the Gateway to Pura Vida | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Poás & Irazú volcanoes, Doka & Café Britt coffee estates, the Gold & Jade museums, and Pacuare whitewater — all day-trippable from SJO. The accurate guide to Costa Rica''s Central Valley gateway. TravelWell.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San José Costa Rica","Volcán Poás tour","tour de café Costa Rica","Volcán Irazú desde San José","Museo del Oro Precolombino","rafting río Pacuare un día","hoteles cerca del aeropuerto Juan Santamaría","Barrio Escalante dónde comer"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicM